        "original_id": "c457d953-4f78-5f78-817e-6ca4409565fd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Jankel, Elton John, Oliver Reed\n- Products: Panther De Ville\n- Topics: British film acting careers\n\nFacts:\n- Oliver Reed was born on 13 February 1938 and died on 2 May 1999.\n- Oliver Reed was an English actor known for an upper-middle-class macho image, a hellraiser lifestyle, and tough-guy roles.\n- Oliver Reed appeared in the films “Women in Love” and “Hannibal Brooks” in 1969.\n- Oliver Reed appeared in the film “The Devils” in 1971.\n- Oliver Reed appeared in the film “The Three Musketeers” in 1973.\n- Oliver Reed appeared in the film “Tommy” in 1975.\n- Oliver Reed appeared in the film “Lion of the Desert” in 1981.\n- Oliver Reed appeared in the film “Castaway” in 1986.\n- Oliver Reed appeared in “The Adventures of Baron Munchausen” in 1988 and “Funny Bones” in 1995.\n- Robert Jankel conceived the Panther De Ville to appeal to nouveau riche customers, including Elton John and Oliver Reed.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "99cc5c77-a196-5f92-9050-40b993c6648e",
        "text": "Page: Panther De Ville. Sentence: The De Ville was conceived by Robert Jankel to appeal to the taste of nouveau riche customers, including singer Elton John and actor Oliver Reed.\nPage: Oliver Reed. Sentence: Robert Oliver Reed (13 February 1938 – 2 May 1999) was an English actor known for his upper-middle class, macho image, hellraiser lifestyle, and \"tough guy\" roles.\nPage: Oliver Reed. Sentence: \" (1968), \"Women in Love\" (1969), \"Hannibal Brooks\" (1969), \"The Devils\" (1971), \"The Three Musketeers\" (1973), \"Tommy\" (1975), \"Lion of the Desert\" (1981), \"Castaway\" (1986), \"The Adventures of Baron Munchausen\" (1988) and \"Funny Bones\" (1995).",
